Work on creating the best editor experience possible. Think about what to improve, which may be anything from optimizations, new features to bug fixes or general QoL. Between every new change I want you to commit and push it to remote. You will have full executive control over the project and you should trust your own instinct. After every hour (set some type of alert), I want you to finish up what you are working on, commit, then send a background fable 5 agent to review the commits since the last review (excluding this first big one). Then work on it's feedback when it comes back. You may continue working whilst your review is in progress.
